# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000022> (ptx homeobox protein)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15895993") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000022> "A protein that has a core domain composition consisting of an N-terminal K50 class Homeobox domain (Pfam:PF00046) and a C-terminal OAR domain (Pfam:PF03826). The homeobox domain consists of a self-folding, stable protein domain of 60 amino acids in which position 50 can confer a distinct DNA binding specificity. The K50 class of homeodomains recognizes a consensus DNA sequence of TAATCC. Homeodomain-containing proteins are known to play important roles in such diverse activities as embryonic pattern formation, cell-type specification, and differentiation.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000022> "PIRSF:PIRSF000563")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasOBONamespace> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000022> "protein")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#id> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000022> "PR:000000022")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000022> "Category=family.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000022> "ptx homeobox protein")
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000022> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_36080>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000023> (retinoblastoma-like protein)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PRO:CNA") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000023> "A protein that has a core domain composition consisting of a Retinoblastoma-associated protein A domain (Pfam:PF01858) followed by a Retinoblastoma-associated protein B domain (Pfam:PF01857). The retinoblastoma-like proteins are key regulators of entry into cell division. They are directly involved in heterochromatin formation by maintaining overall chromatin structure and, in particular, that of constitutive heterochromatin by stabilizing histone methylation.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000023> "PIRSF:PIRSF037408")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasOBONamespace> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000023> "protein")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#id> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000023> "PR:000000023")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000023> "Category=family.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000023> "retinoblastoma-like protein")
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000023> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_36080>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000024> (Rho-associated protein kinase)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PRO:CNA") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000024> "A protein that is a translation product of an evolutionary-related gene with core domain composition consisting of an N-terminal Protein kinase domain (Pfam:PF00069), a Rho Binding domain (Pfam:PF08912), and a PH domain (Pfam:PF00169) and a Phorbol esters/diacylglycerol binding domain (C1 domain) (Pfam:PF00130) at the C-terminus. Rho-associated protein kinases are mediators of many cellular processes by being effectors of the small GTP-binding protein Rho.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000024> "PIRSF:PIRSF037568")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasOBONamespace> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000024> "protein")
