SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000547> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002353> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0016485>))

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000668> (calcium-activated calmodulin-binding potassium channel alpha subunit)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:10026195") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11323678") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000668> "A calcium-activated potassium channel protein that has amino- and carboxyl-terminal intracellular domains separated by a domain containing six transmembrane helices (S1-S6) in which the last two helices (S5 and S6) flank a loop, called the pore loop, which determines ion selectivity. They are subunits of the small conductance calcium-activated channels. SK channels are independent of voltage and gated solely by intracellular calcium. These membrane channels are heteromeric complexes that comprise pore-forming alpha-subunits and the calcium-binding protein calmodulin. Calmodulin binds to the SK channel through the Calmodulin binding domain (Pfam:PF02888), which is located in an intracellular region of the alpha-subunit immediately carboxy-terminal to the pore. Channel opening is triggered when calcium binds the EF hands in the N-lobe of calmodulin. These channels play a crucial role in hyperpolarizing the membrane potential of excitable and nonexcitable cells.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000668> "PIRSF:PIRSF038511")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasOBONamespace> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000668> "protein")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#id> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000668> "PR:000000668")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000668> "Category=family.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000668> "calcium-activated calmodulin-binding potassium channel alpha subunit")
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000668> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000044649>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000673> (cyclic nucleotide-gated channel alpha subunit)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12432397") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PRO:CNA") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000673> "A cyclic nucleotide-regulated channel protein that has amino- and carboxyl-terminal intracellular domains separated by a domain (common with other ion channels) containing six transmembrane helices (S1-S6) in which the last two helices (S5 and S6) flank a loop, called the pore loop, which determines ion selectivity. The carboxy-terminal region contains the Cyclic nucleotide-binding domain (Pfam:PF00027) (CNBD) and a region connecting the CNBD to the S6 segment (C-linker), which is important for modulation by transition metals. In addition, CNG alpha has a carboxy-terminal leucine zipper that seems to be involved in inter-subunit interaction. CNG alpha subunits combine with the beta subunits to form the cyclic nucleotide-gated ion channels, which mediate sensory transduction in photoreceptors and olfactory sensory neurons. These channels are likely composed of four subunits around a centrally located ion-permeable pore that opens in response to the direct binding of intracellular cyclic nucleotides. CNG channels are non-selective cation channels. They are not gated by membrane voltage although their structure includes the transmembrane S4 motif known to function as the membrane voltage sensor in all voltage-gated ion channels, but it has been shown to be important for proper folding and processing. Alpha and beta subunits of the CNG channel are very similar, however only alpha subunits are able to homooligomerize and form functional channels.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000673> "PIRSF:PIRSF002403")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasOBONamespace> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000673> "protein")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#id> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000673> "PR:000000673")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000673> "Category=family.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000673> "cyclic nucleotide-gated channel alpha subunit")
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000673> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000044648>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000674> (cyclic nucleotide-gated channel beta subunit)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PRO:CNA") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000674> "A cyclic nucleotide-regulated channel protein that is the modulatory subunit of the cyclic nucleotide-gated channel (CNG channel). It consists of amino- and carboxyl-terminal intracellular domains separated by a domain (common with other ion channels) containing six transmembrane helices (S1-S6) in which the last two helices (S5 and S6) flank a loop, called the pore loop, which determines ion selectivity. The carboxy-terminal region contains the Cyclic nucleotide-binding domain (Pfam:PF00027) (CNBD) and a region connecting the CNBD to the S6 segment (C-linker), which is important for modulation by transition metals. CNG beta subunits combine with the alpha subunits to form the cyclic nucleotide-gated ion channels, which mediate sensory transduction in photoreceptors and olfactory sensory neurons. These channels are likely composed of four subunits around a centrally located ion-permeable pore that opens in response to the direct binding of intracellular cyclic nucleotides. CNG channels are non-selective cation channels. They are not gated by membrane voltage although their structure includes the transmembrane S4 motif known to function as the membrane voltage sensor in all voltage-gated ion channels, but it has been shown to be important for proper folding and processing. Alpha and beta subunits of the CNG channel are very similar, however the beta subunits are not able to form functional channels by themselves.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000674> "PIRSF:PIRSF038515")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasOBONamespace> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000674> "protein")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#id> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000674> "PR:000000674")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000674> "Category=family.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000674> "cyclic nucleotide-gated channel beta subunit")
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000674> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000044648>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000675> (platelet-derived growth factor with CUB domain)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PRO:CNA") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000000675> "A protein that has a core domain composition consisting of a signal peptide, a CUB domain (Pfam:PF00431), and a C-terminal Platelet-derived growth factor (PDGF) domain (Pfam:PF00341).")
