# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000001353> (granulocyte colony-stimulating factor receptor)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:1723014") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PRO:CNA") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000001353> "A protein that is a translation product of the human CSF3R gene or a 1:1 ortholog thereof. The active receptor is a homodimer which can bind G-CSF and transduce G-CSF-triggered growth signals into cells. Its extracellular domain contains a sequence of about 200 amino acids which can be found in various cytokine receptors. In addition, it contains an immunoglobulin-like domain and three fibronectin type III domains.")
